15 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting patient selection for a study. Initially, 150 patients over eighteen underwent thyroid surgery. Fifty-seven were excluded for reasons like incomplete records, previous surgery, inadequate imaging, or lack of preoperative ultrasound. Ninety-three patients with 101 nodules were classified using the ACR TI-RADS/C-TIRADS framework. Thirty-eight benign cases were further excluded, leaving 63 cases for LLMs input.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Bar chart titled \215Kappa Consistency: Expert vs Models \(ACR & C-TIRADS\)\216 comparing Cohen's kappa values for models GPT-4o, GPT-o3-mini, and DeepSeek-R1 using two grading systems: ACR \(blue\) and C-TIRADS \(pink\). GPT-4o and GPT-o3-mini have ACR kappa of 0.614 and DeepSeek-R1 has 0.480. C-TIRADS values are 0.212, 0.368, and 0.223 respectively. Error bars indicate variability.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (ROC curves comparing different diagnostic models based on their grade. The true positive rate is plotted against the false positive rate. The models include Expert ACR, Expert C-TIRADS, GPT-4o ACR, GPT-4o C-TIRADS, GPT-3-mini ACR, GPT-3-mini C-TIRADS, DeepSeek-R1 ACR, and DeepSeek-R1 C-TIRADS. The AUC values are shown in the legend, with Expert ACR showing the highest AUC of 0.900.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Bar chart panels comparing evaluations of ACR-TIRADS and C-TIRADS by surgeons and endocrinologists. Metrics include guideline adherence, patient safety, operational feasibility, clinical applicability, and overall performance. Each panel shows mean scores for models: DeepSeek-R1, GPT-4o, and GPT-3o-mini.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
